}
```

The Miaoda agent is accessible at `https://miaoda.feishu.cn/app/app_4jpd2jyqtwqgt/`. But this is the OpenClaw web interface, not a VNC/browsing session.


The real blocker is that this server in mainland China can't reach Google's services, and NotebookLM is a Google product entirely hosted on Google's infrastructure. So my options are either finding a VPN or proxy to bypass the Great Firewall, switching to an alternative like Coze that works within China's network restrictions, or storing auth tokens locally and syncing them somehow.

Actually, I'm realizing the Miaoda Cloud Computer might already have browser functionality built in that could route through a different network path—let me investigate whether the OpenClaw browser tool can actually help here.

